# This is a sample tab separated file of IMDb tconst IDs to be processed
#       See https://www.imdb.com/interfaces/ for a description of IMDb datasets
#       tconst (string) - alphanumeric unique identifier of the title
#
# The tconst for any show can be found in its IMDb URL -- e.g. the URL for
# "The Crown" is:
#       https://www.imdb.com/title/tt4786824/

# Create a similar tconst file of shows you've watched or are interested in. If
# it has a .tconst extension, it will be automatically processed. However it can
# have any name and extension and be passed as a parameter on the command line,
# e.g. Netflix.tconst.txt

# Your tconst file only needs to contain the tconst field and any comments you'd
# like. Running ./augment_tconstFiles.sh -i will fill in the other fields for
# you.

# Only the tconst field is used. Additional fields are not needed, but useful
# for documentation.

# tconst	Type	Primary Title	Original Title	Date
tt4786824	tvSeries	The Crown	The Crown	2016
tt5014882	tvSeries	The Durrells	The Durrells	2016
tt1399664	tvSeries	The Night Manager	The Night Manager	2016
